.TH LAZYTUI 1 "2026-09-20" "caveutils" "caveutils Manual"
.SH NAME
lazytui \- a reusable lazy-loading fzf front-end.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lazytui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lazytui
.nf

  lazytui --seed CMD [--more CMD] [--reload CMD] [--preview CMD]
          [--accept CMD] [--key N] [--nth LIST] [--header STR] [--prompt STR]

  --seed CMD     stdout is the initial list, shown at once (fast). required.
  --more CMD     stdout replaces the list when ready (slow) - run in the
                 background, swapped in live via fzf's --listen port.
  --reload CMD   run on every query change ({q} = current query) - stdout
                 replaces the list. The "search as you type" hook.
  --preview CMD  `CMD <key>` fills the preview pane for the highlighted row.
  --accept CMD   Enter runs `CMD <key>`, replacing the TUI (fzf `become`).
                 Omitted -> the key is printed to stdout and lazytui exits.
  --key N        which TAB-separated field is the row's key (default 1).
  --nth LIST     fzf --with-nth (default: everything).

TAB is the delimiter. Plain fzf underneath - Ctrl-C / Esc quit.
.fi
